                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac914bc4-6464-3748-b67f-6bf5ce6ed8ea",
                        "entry_id": "850983a8-a690-3363-9f0e-c427ca97d5b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having or relating to an unsatisfactory form of immortality accompanied by aging and disease."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7fa8391-2883-4e57-a5ff-2d453e10b145",
                                "sense_id": "ac914bc4-6464-3748-b67f-6bf5ce6ed8ea",
                                "text": "The methods employed to select economic and political leaders must be modified in a manner suited to allow, in the future, a sufficient number of places to those under (say) fifty; otherwise, given both present methods of selection and prospective changes in age composition, too much power may pass into the hands of gerontocrats with a Struldbruggian incapacity for fashioning or selecting economic and political policies suited to the needs of the times."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f143c25d-d123-4205-8e29-fbebee278d53",
                                "sense_id": "ac914bc4-6464-3748-b67f-6bf5ce6ed8ea",
                                "text": "Here are all the elements of a truly creative scepticism blended for once into a manageable and yet an infinitely expandable pattern. It might have required at least ten more years (if Adams could have counted on escaping Struldbruggian senescence) for him to set this insight to work."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6fd9301-2968-4d8d-a70c-cec1aade993e",
                                "sense_id": "ac914bc4-6464-3748-b67f-6bf5ce6ed8ea",
                                "text": "Critics of techniques to lengthen the human life span often paint a Struldbruggian picture of our future. In these scenarios, a large elderly population is kept alive only through incredibly expensive medical techniques paid for by the young."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
